<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-all</AnalysisLevel>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <Company>Your Organization</Company>
    <Authors>Your Organization</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026</Copyright>
    <NeutralLanguage>en</NeutralLanguage>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <ProduceReferenceAssembly>true</ProduceReferenceAssembly>

    <!--
      AnalysisLevel is "latest-all", the strictest setting, which surfaces a number of rules that
      don't fit this library and are suppressed deliberately below rather than by weakening
      AnalysisLevel itself:
        CA1028 - byte-backed enums are intentional: these enums model exact 1-byte wire values
                 from the ACR122U spec (key types, PICC parameters, LED flags, etc.), and casting
                 to/from byte is the whole point.
        CA1008 - a required "zero-value member" doesn't make sense for enums that mirror specific
                 non-zero protocol byte values (e.g. KeyType.TypeA = 0x60).
        CA1711 - "LedControlFlags" ending in "Flags" is the clearest possible name for what it is.
        CA1027 - ContactlessModulationType is a discrete PN532 enum value, not a bit-flag set.
        CA1024 - the Acr122uCommands builder methods return a *new* CommandApdu each call and read
                 more naturally as verbs ("GetUid()") than as properties.
        CA1815 - ResponseApdu is a short-lived transport value never used in equality comparisons
                 or collections; adding Equals/== would be unused surface area.
        CA1819 - AtrInfo.Raw/HistoricalBytes intentionally expose raw byte buffers; this is a
                 low-level protocol library where copying defensively on every access isn't worth
                 the cost, and callers are expected to treat them as read-only.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1028;CA1008;CA1711;CA1027;CA1024;CA1815;CA1819</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
